      "message": "Add a comment that this codepath is special? For example:\n\n    // Called by getFirstKey. Find the first key in the map.\n\nThat said - is this correct? If a caller calls getFirstKey, and the map is empty, presumably we need to return null without throwing an exception. We should ensure that this code can handle that.\n\nDo we have tests for this case? If not, we should. In fact, I think we need tests for at least the following cases.\n\n - getFirstKey on empty map: returns null\n - getFirstKey on non-empty map: returns first key\n - getNextKey with null key: behaves like getFirstKey. Actually, I\u0027m not sure we should allow users to do this at all, see comment on BpfMap.java.\n - getNextKey with non-existent key: returns first key (would be nice if this could throw enoent, but I think we can\u0027t because the kernel won\u0027t tell us)\n - getNextKey with (existing) non-last key: returns next key\n - getNextKey with (existing) last key: returns null\n - getNextKey with non-null (non-existent) key on empty map: returns null",
