      "message": "Given the way the code is written, I believe that the consumer must not delete the key (because that will cause iteration to restart from the beginning of the map). If so, you should document that clearly in the docstring.\n\nHowever, I think it\u0027s actually possible to make it work. Something like this, maybe?\n\n        @Nullable K nextKey \u003d getFirstKey();\n        while (nextKey !\u003d null) {\n            @NonNull final K curKey \u003d nextKey;\n            @NonNull final V value \u003d getValue(curKey);\n            nextKey \u003d getNextKey(curKey);\n            action.accept(curKey, value);\n        }\n\nIf this does works, then say in the docstring that the consumer is allowed to delete the key, but any other delete operations while this method is running are not allowed and will result in undefined behaviour.\n\nOf course, this needs to be covered by the test.",
